  "body": "In #827 the idea came up that now that we have unions we could handle null in a generalized way. That is, rather than `DOMString?`, you would write `(DOMString or null)`.\r\n\r\nI like that this adds a lot of clarity with regards to the allowed values, but I do worry a bit about the verbosity. We might want to add a typedef for `NullableDOMString` or some such.",
